IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc1-support`

-- ccc1-s33-45-defences.l4 -- Part I (General), sections 33.1 to 45: self-induced extreme intoxication, defence of person, defence of property, correction of a child by force,
-- surgical operations; sections 36 to 42 and 44 are shown repealed.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- A defence ("is not guilty", "is justified", "is protected"): where its "if" gate is not met the answer is JUST FALSE, read as "this section gives no defence on these facts" and never as "no defence at all"
-- (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)); a "who" description not met answers NOTHING. A "does not apply" subsection (34(3), 35(2), 35(3)) is named as a bar: JUST TRUE = the defence does not apply.
-- The open-textured judgments ("reasonable in the circumstances", "reasonable grounds", "departed markedly from the standard of care") are INPUTS the person states; the factors the court must consider are listed as functions.
-- Section 33.1 liability turns on "extreme intoxication" (33.1(4)) and on the offences of 33.1(3): both answers are inputs here (MAYBE BOOLEAN), computed by the functions of the same section.

§ `Section 33.1 -- Self-induced extreme intoxication`

-- src:785 | Self-induced Extreme Intoxication
-- src:786 | Offences of violence by negligence
-- src:787 | 33.1 (1) A person who, by reason of self-induced extreme intoxication, lacks the general intent or voluntariness ordinarily required to commit an offence referred to in subsection (3), nonetheless commits the offence if
-- src:788 | (a) all the other elements of the offence are present; and
-- src:789 | (b) before they were in a state of extreme intoxication, they departed markedly from the standard of care expected of a reasonable person in the circumstances with respect to the consumption of intoxicating substances.
@ref s 33.1(1) (src:785-789)
GIVEN `the person lacks the general intent or voluntariness ordinarily required to commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that is by reason of self-induced extreme intoxication, by s 33.1(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 33.1(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `all the other elements of the offence are present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before they were in a state of extreme intoxication, they departed markedly from the standard of care expected of a reasonable person in the circumstances with respect to the consumption of intoxicating substances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33.1(1) the person nonetheless commits the offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person lacks the general intent or voluntariness ordinarily required to commit the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who, by reason of self-induced extreme intoxication, lacks the general intent or voluntariness ordinarily required to commit an offence referred to in subsection (3)"
        IF `that is by reason of self-induced extreme intoxication, by s 33.1(4)` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the offence is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 33.1(3)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) or (4) did not answer whether the offence is one referred to in (3) or the intoxication is extreme intoxication
        IF (`that is by reason of self-induced extreme intoxication, by s 33.1(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the offence is one referred to in subsection (3), by s 33.1(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason of self-induced extreme intoxication" "an offence referred to in subsection (3)"
        IF `all the other elements of the offence are present` AND `before they were in a state of extreme intoxication, they departed markedly from the standard of care expected of a reasonable person in the circumstances with respect to the consumption of intoxicating substances` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nonetheless commits the offence if (a) all the other elements of the offence are present; and (b) before they were in a state of extreme intoxication"

-- src:790 | Marked departure — foreseeability of risk and other circumstances
-- src:791 | (2) For the purposes of determining whether the person departed markedly from the standard of care, the court must consider the objective foreseeability of the risk that the consumption of the intoxicating substances could cause extreme intoxication and lead the person to harm another person. The court must, in making the determination, also consider all relevant circumstances, including anything that the person did to avoid the risk.
@ref s 33.1(2) (src:790-791)
DECLARE `s 33.1(2) the matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 33.1(2) the objective foreseeability of the risk that the consumption of the intoxicating substances could cause extreme intoxication and lead the person to harm another person`
    `s 33.1(2) all relevant circumstances, including anything that the person did to avoid the risk`
    `s 33.1(2) another matter`

DECLARE `s 33.1(2) the act the duty is to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 33.1(2) consider the objective foreseeability of the risk that the consumption of the intoxicating substances could cause extreme intoxication and lead the person to harm another person`
    `s 33.1(2) consider all relevant circumstances, including anything that the person did to avoid the risk`

@ref s 33.1(2) (src:790-791)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether the person departed markedly from the standard of care` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 33.1(2) the matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33.1(2) the court must consider the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is determining whether the person departed markedly from the standard of care` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of determining whether the person departed markedly from the standard of care"
        IF matter EQUALS `s 33.1(2) another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "all relevant circumstances, including anything that the person did to avoid the risk"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 33.1(2) (src:790-791)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 33.1(2) the act the duty is to do`
`s 33.1(2) the duty of the court to consider the objective foreseeability of the risk` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 33.1(2) consider the objective foreseeability of the risk that the consumption of the intoxicating substances could cause extreme intoxication and lead the person to harm another person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the court did not consider the objective foreseeability of the risk"

@ref s 33.1(2) (src:790-791)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 33.1(2) the act the duty is to do`
`s 33.1(2) the duty of the court to consider all relevant circumstances` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 33.1(2) consider all relevant circumstances, including anything that the person did to avoid the risk`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the court did not consider all relevant circumstances, including anything that the person did to avoid the risk"

-- src:792 | Offences
-- src:793 | (3) This section applies in respect of an offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament that includes as an element an assault or any other interference or threat of interference by a person with the bodily integrity of another person.
@ref s 33.1(3) (src:792-793)
GIVEN `the offence is under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it includes as an element an assault or any other interference or threat of interference by a person with the bodily integrity of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33.1(3) section 33.1 applies in respect of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence is under this Act or any other Act of Parliament` AND `it includes as an element an assault or any other interference or threat of interference by a person with the bodily integrity of another person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under this Act or any other Act of Parliament that includes as an element an assault or any other interference or threat of interference by a person with the bodily integrity of another person"

-- src:794 | Definition of extreme intoxication
-- src:795 | (4) In this section, extreme intoxication means intoxication that renders a person unaware of, or incapable of consciously controlling, their behaviour.
@ref s 33.1(4) (src:794-795)
GIVEN `it is intoxication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it renders a person unaware of their behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it renders a person incapable of consciously controlling their behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33.1(4) extreme intoxication` MEANS
    IF `it is intoxication` AND (`it renders a person unaware of their behaviour` OR `it renders a person incapable of consciously controlling their behaviour`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "extreme intoxication means intoxication that renders a person unaware of, or incapable of consciously controlling, their behaviour"

§ `Section 34 -- Defence of person`

-- src:797 | Defence of Person
-- src:798 | Defence — use or threat of force
-- src:799 | 34 (1) A person is not guilty of an offence if
-- src:800 | (a) they believe on reasonable grounds that force is being used against them or another person or that a threat of force is being made against them or another person;
-- src:801 | (b) the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of defending or protecting themselves or the other person from that use or threat of force; and
-- src:802 | (c) the act committed is reasonable in the circumstances.
@ref s 34(1) (src:797-802)
GIVEN `they believe on reasonable grounds that force is being used against them or another person or that a threat of force is being made against them or another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of defending or protecting themselves or the other person from that use or threat of force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act committed is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(1) the person is not guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `they believe on reasonable grounds that force is being used against them or another person or that a threat of force is being made against them or another person`
       AND `the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of defending or protecting themselves or the other person from that use or threat of force`
       AND `the act committed is reasonable in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not guilty of an offence if (a) they believe on reasonable grounds that force is being used against them or another person or that a threat of force is being made against them or another person"

-- src:803 | Factors
-- src:804 | (2) In determining whether the act committed is reasonable in the circumstances, the court shall consider the relevant circumstances of the person, the other parties and the act, including, but not limited to, the following factors:
-- src:805 | (a) the nature of the force or threat;
-- src:806 | (b) the extent to which the use of force was imminent and whether there were other means available to respond to the potential use of force;
-- src:807 | (c) the person’s role in the incident;
-- src:808 | (d) whether any party to the incident used or threatened to use a weapon;
-- src:809 | (e) the size, age, gender and physical capabilities of the parties to the incident;
-- src:810 | (f) the nature, duration and history of any relationship between the parties to the incident, including any prior use or threat of force and the nature of that force or threat;
-- src:811 | (f.1) any history of interaction or communication between the parties to the incident;
-- src:812 | (g) the nature and proportionality of the person’s response to the use or threat of force; and
-- src:813 | (h) whether the act committed was in response to a use or threat of force that the person knew was lawful.
@ref s 34(2) (src:803-813)
DECLARE `s 34(2) the factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 34(2)(a) the nature of the force or threat`
    `s 34(2)(b) the extent to which the use of force was imminent and whether there were other means available to respond to the potential use of force`
    `s 34(2)(c) the person’s role in the incident`
    `s 34(2)(d) whether any party to the incident used or threatened to use a weapon`
    `s 34(2)(e) the size, age, gender and physical capabilities of the parties to the incident`
    `s 34(2)(f) the nature, duration and history of any relationship between the parties to the incident, including any prior use or threat of force and the nature of that force or threat`
    `s 34(2)(f.1) any history of interaction or communication between the parties to the incident`
    `s 34(2)(g) the nature and proportionality of the person’s response to the use or threat of force`
    `s 34(2)(h) whether the act committed was in response to a use or threat of force that the person knew was lawful`
    `s 34(2) another circumstance of the person, the other parties or the act`

@ref s 34(2) (src:803-813)
GIVEN factor IS A `s 34(2) the factor`
      `it is a relevant circumstance of the person, the other parties or the act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(2) the court shall consider the factor` MEANS
    IF factor EQUALS `s 34(2) another circumstance of the person, the other parties or the act`
    THEN (IF `it is a relevant circumstance of the person, the other parties or the act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court shall consider the relevant circumstances of the person, the other parties and the act"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:814 | No defence
-- src:815 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply if the force is used or threatened by another person for the purpose of doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law, unless the person who commits the act that constitutes the offence believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully.
@ref s 34(3) (src:814-815)
GIVEN `the force is used or threatened by another person for the purpose of doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who commits the act that constitutes the offence believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34(3) subsection (1) does not apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the force is used or threatened by another person for the purpose of doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the force is used or threatened by another person for the purpose of doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law"
        IF `the person who commits the act that constitutes the offence believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the person who commits the act that constitutes the offence believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 34(1), (3) (a composition of two subsections: no quotation)
GIVEN `the answer of subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of subsection (3): subsection (1) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34 the person is not guilty of the offence, subject to subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the answer of subsection (3): subsection (1) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the force is used or threatened by another person"
    ELSE `the answer of subsection (1)`

§ `Section 35 -- Defence of property`

-- src:817 | Defence of Property
-- src:818 | Defence — property
-- src:819 | 35 (1) A person is not guilty of an offence if
-- src:820 | (a) they either believe on reasonable grounds that they are in peaceable possession of property or are acting under the authority of, or lawfully assisting, a person whom they believe on reasonable grounds is in peaceable possession of property;
-- src:821 | (b) they believe on reasonable grounds that another person
-- src:822 | (i) is about to enter, is entering or has entered the property without being entitled by law to do so,
-- src:823 | (ii) is about to take the property, is doing so or has just done so, or
-- src:824 | (iii) is about to damage or destroy the property, or make it inoperative, or is doing so;
-- src:825 | (c) the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of
-- src:826 | (i) preventing the other person from entering the property, or removing that person from the property, or
-- src:827 | (ii) preventing the other person from taking, damaging or destroying the property or from making it inoperative, or retaking the property from that person; and
-- src:828 | (d) the act committed is reasonable in the circumstances.
@ref s 35(1) (src:817-828)
GIVEN `they believe on reasonable grounds that they are in peaceable possession of property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are acting under the authority of, or lawfully assisting, a person whom they believe on reasonable grounds is in peaceable possession of property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to enter, is entering or has entered the property without being entitled by law to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to take the property, is doing so or has just done so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to damage or destroy the property, or make it inoperative, or is doing so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of preventing the other person from entering the property, or removing that person from the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of preventing the other person from taking, damaging or destroying the property or from making it inoperative, or retaking the property from that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act committed is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(1) the person is not guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF (`they believe on reasonable grounds that they are in peaceable possession of property` OR `they are acting under the authority of, or lawfully assisting, a person whom they believe on reasonable grounds is in peaceable possession of property`)
       AND (`they believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to enter, is entering or has entered the property without being entitled by law to do so`
            OR `they believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to take the property, is doing so or has just done so`
            OR `they believe on reasonable grounds that another person is about to damage or destroy the property, or make it inoperative, or is doing so`)
       AND (`the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of preventing the other person from entering the property, or removing that person from the property`
            OR `the act that constitutes the offence is committed for the purpose of preventing the other person from taking, damaging or destroying the property or from making it inoperative, or retaking the property from that person`)
       AND `the act committed is reasonable in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not guilty of an offence if (a) they either believe on reasonable grounds that they are in peaceable possession of property"

-- src:829 | No defence
-- src:830 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the person who believes on reasonable grounds that they are, or who is believed on reasonable grounds to be, in peaceable possession of the property does not have a claim of right to it and the other person is entitled to its possession by law.
@ref s 35(2) (src:829-830)
GIVEN `the person who believes on reasonable grounds that they are, or who is believed on reasonable grounds to be, in peaceable possession of the property does not have a claim of right to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is entitled to its possession by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(2) subsection (1) does not apply because the other person is entitled to possession` MEANS
    IF `the person who believes on reasonable grounds that they are, or who is believed on reasonable grounds to be, in peaceable possession of the property does not have a claim of right to it` AND `the other person is entitled to its possession by law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the person who believes on reasonable grounds that they are, or who is believed on reasonable grounds to be, in peaceable possession of the property does not have a claim of right to it and the other person is entitled to its possession by law"

-- src:831 | No defence
-- src:832 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply if the other person is doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law, unless the person who commits the act that constitutes the offence believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully.
@ref s 35(3) (src:831-832)
GIVEN `the other person is doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who commits the act that constitutes the offence believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(3) subsection (1) does not apply because the other person is acting in the administration or enforcement of the law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the other person is doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the other person is doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law"
        IF `the person who commits the act that constitutes the offence believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the person who commits the act that constitutes the offence believes on reasonable grounds that the other person is acting unlawfully"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 35(1), (2), (3) (a composition of three subsections: no quotation)
GIVEN `the answer of subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of subsection (2): subsection (1) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of subsection (3): subsection (1) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35 the person is not guilty of the offence, subject to subsections (2) and (3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of subsection (2): subsection (1) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the person who believes on reasonable grounds that they are, or who is believed on reasonable grounds to be, in peaceable possession of the property does not have a claim of right to it"
        IF `the answer of subsection (3): subsection (1) does not apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the other person is doing something that they are required or authorized by law to do in the administration or enforcement of the law"
        OTHERWISE `the answer of subsection (1)`

