§ `Sections 43 to 45 -- Protection of persons in authority; surgical operations`

-- src:841 | Protection of Persons in Authority
-- src:842 | Correction of child by force
-- src:843 | 43 Every schoolteacher, parent or person standing in the place of a parent is justified in using force by way of correction toward a pupil or child, as the case may be, who is under his care, if the force does not exceed what is reasonable under the circumstances.
@ref s 43 (src:841-843)
DECLARE `s 43 the person is` IS ONE OF
    `s 43 a schoolteacher`
    `s 43 a parent`
    `s 43 a person standing in the place of a parent`
    `s 43 another person`

@ref s 43 (src:841-843)
GIVEN who IS A `s 43 the person is`
      `the pupil or child is under their care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force is used by way of correction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the force does not exceed what is reasonable under the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43 the person is justified in using force by way of correction toward the pupil or child` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF who EQUALS `s 43 another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every schoolteacher, parent or person standing in the place of a parent"
        IF NOT (`the pupil or child is under their care` AND `the force is used by way of correction`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "using force by way of correction toward a pupil or child, as the case may be, who is under his care"
        IF `the force does not exceed what is reasonable under the circumstances` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the force does not exceed what is reasonable under the circumstances"

-- src:844 | 44 [Repealed, 2001, c. 26, s. 294]
@ref s 44 (src:844-844)
`s 44 as the text shows it` MEANS "[Repealed, 2001, c. 26, s. 294]"

-- src:845 | Surgical operations
-- src:846 | 45 Every one is protected from criminal responsibility for performing a surgical operation on any person for the benefit of that person if
-- src:847 | (a) the operation is performed with reasonable care and skill; and
-- src:848 | (b) it is reasonable to perform the operation, having regard to the state of health of the person at the time the operation is performed and to all the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 45 (src:845-848)
GIVEN `the person performs a surgical operation on any person for the benefit of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the operation is performed with reasonable care and skill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is reasonable to perform the operation, having regard to the state of health of the person at the time the operation is performed and to all the circumstances of the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45 the person is protected from criminal responsibility for performing the surgical operation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person performs a surgical operation on any person for the benefit of that person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for performing a surgical operation on any person for the benefit of that person"
        IF `the operation is performed with reasonable care and skill` AND `it is reasonable to perform the operation, having regard to the state of health of the person at the time the operation is performed and to all the circumstances of the case` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is protected from criminal responsibility for performing a surgical operation on any person for the benefit of that person if"
